{"id": "EUVD-2026-96399", "enisaUuid": "e447884f-67c3-3ae5-a2e1-c8ce7c2fb894", "description": "Phi 0.3.0 through 0.28.4 contains a permission bypass vulnerability that allows spawned sub-agents to escape workspace_only_writes and readonly mode by supplying an unchecked workdir to agent_spawn. Attackers can plant prompt-injected instructions in processed content so the agent spawns a worker rooted elsewhere, causing unapproved file writes anywhere the user can write.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T18:16:58", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T18:56:08", "baseScore": 6.0, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind/phi-subagent-workdir-workspace-escape", "https://github.com/pulseaiclub/phi/blob/5b3cb440a7c58115ef64283a737a43299f2805a4/internal/tools/agenttool/agent.go#L106-L120", "https://github.com/pulseaiclub/phi/blob/5b3cb440a7c58115ef64283a737a43299f2805a4/internal/agent/engine_runner.go#L52-L60", "https://github.com/pulseaiclub/phi", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/phi-0.3.0-through-0.28.4-permission-bypass-via-agent-spawn-workdir"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108595", "GHSA-x8rp-9mrq-5584"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.26, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ee9b0447-1166-374e-943f-01d7aad7d68e", "product": {"name": "phi", "vendor": {"name": "pulseaiclub"}}, "product_version": "0.3.0 \u22640.28.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f6979e8f-b761-3019-ac05-5a9e2e43879b", "vendor": {"name": "pulseaiclub"}}], "isExploited": false}